      "message": "If I\u0027m reading that correctly it\u0027s building a key for each individual message in a batch?  If it is then I\u0027m not certain that the Python version we\u0027re using right now has that capability.  It accepts a key for any message, or list of messages, that you write to Kafka but to get the performance we want we need to write as many as possible at once.\n\nThere have been quite a few improvements in the python kafka library since we froze on 0.9.2 so it\u0027s possible we can do what the Java library is doing with more recent versions.\n\nWould the current method of distribution be sufficient for the Threshold engine?  It was sufficient for the Notification engine and should be sufficient for the Persister.",
